 "/evidence-library/newspaper-transcriptions/": {
  "title": "Newspaper Transcriptions",
  "html": "<p class=\"meta\">Legal Wiki page 929 · page in the WordPress bin · last edited 2026-10-05 · copied to Research 24 October 2026 so the text survives the wiki’s retirement</p><p>Status: working index. The South Wales Echo entries below are catalogued from the working text in the datro archive (“Bpvsbucker Rundown”). Their images have not yet been visually checked, so none of them is a verified transcription. The evidence label column (Record / Family acc…</p><details><summary>Full page text</summary><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Status: working index.</strong> The South Wales Echo entries below are catalogued from the working text in the datro archive (&#8220;Bpvsbucker Rundown&#8221;). Their images have not yet been visually checked, so none of them is a verified transcription. The evidence label column (Record / Family account / Contention) is still to be completed.</p><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Items with an image in the media library</h2><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li><a href=\"/?page_id=927\">1974 article (media ID 479)</a>: transcription pending</li><li><a href=\"/?page_id=928\">1988 &#8220;History Fight to Save Farm&#8221; (media ID 480)</a>: transcription pending</li></ul><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">South Wales Echo, 1988 to 1989 (from the Rundown)</h2><figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Headline or subject</th><th>Image checked</th><th>Evidence label</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>29 Apr 1988</td><td>Legal battle for two generations</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>30 Apr 1988</td><td>Refusing medical check-up</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>12 May 1988</td><td>DRAMA SUCCESS &#8211; MP asks Lord Chancellor</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>30 Nov 1988</td><td>Demolition workers move in</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2 Dec 1988</td><td>High Court ruling and BP Properties demolition</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3 Dec 1988</td><td>Evicted farmer Bill Buckler taken from hospital</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6 Dec 1988</td><td>Mrs Buckler Eviction</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>7 Dec 1988</td><td>Vale of Glamorgan councillor and BP pensioner</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>9 Dec 1988</td><td>Bid to stop BP Properties</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>10 Dec 1988</td><td>Buckler freed on bail</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>13 Dec 1988</td><td>All I&#8217;ve got left</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>21 Dec 1988</td><td>Branwen near the remains</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>6 Jan 1989</td><td>Bail change for evicted farmer</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>11 Feb 1989</td><td>Legal action against BP Properties</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>23 Mar 1989</td><td>Evicted farmer freed after pleading guilty</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>24 Mar 1989</td><td>Harm charge farmer freed: &#8220;I will fight on to the death&#8221;</td><td>No</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Headlines are as listed in the Rundown and may differ from the printed headlines. Which of these correspond to the four placeholder captures on the Media Gallery has not yet been confirmed.</p></details>"
 },
