 "/evidence/mr-0163/": {
  "title": "MR-0163 — sconzani (blog), Apr 2020",
  "notitle": true,
  "html": "<div id=\"mre\"><style>#mre dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;gap:4px 12px;margin:8px 0}#mre dt{color:var(--wiki-muted,#54595d);font-size:.85rem}#mre dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#mre blockquote{margin:8px 0;padding:4px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--wiki-border,#a2a9b1)}#mre .nav a{margin-right:12px;display:inline-block}</style><p class=\"meta\">MR-0163 · Apr 2020 · sconzani (blog)</p><blockquote>sconzani: Llandough : St Dochdwy&#x27;s Church</blockquote><p>Local-history blog post on St Dochdwy&#x27;s Church, Llandough: earlier c.1820 church moved stone by stone to Leckwith; present church consecrated 1866, designed by a Bristol architect, built by a Penarth contractor; cites the Coflein entry.</p><dl><dt>Date</dt><dd>Apr 2020</dd><dt>Outlet</dt><dd>sconzani (blog)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>blog</dd><dt>Access</dt><dd>open</dd><dt>Topics</dt><dd>heritage, church, social</dd></dl><p class=\"nav\"><a href=\"http://sconzani.blogspot.com/2020/04/llandough-st-dochdwys-church.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Source</a> <a href=\"/evidence/media-coverage-1850-2026/#MR-0163\">Media coverage list</a> <a href=\"/timeline/central-chronology/#CH-0016\">Chronology CH-0016</a></p></div>"
 },
