 "/timeline/": "<section class=\"research-addendum\" id=\"research-central-chronology\"><p><a href=\"/timeline/central-chronology/\">Central chronology</a><a href=\"/story/\">The whole story, tagged</a>: 596 dated events, each with its source · <a href=\"/evidence/media-coverage-1850-2026/\">Media coverage 1850–2026</a>: 228 press, TV, video and heritage items</p></section><section class=\"research-addendum\" id=\"research-added-2026-10-23\"><h2>Added on research: 23 October 2026</h2><details><summary>Correspondence 20–23 October 2026 (11 entries)</summary><ul><li><strong>20 Oct 2026</strong> · EIR request to Natural Resources Wales: Cwm Cydfin SSSI notification and owner/occupier records, woodland title WA735527 at Llandough, and the Forestry Commission lease of Leckwith Woods. Reply due 17 Nov 2026. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0514</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a156ae46b1bad14\">email</a></li><li><strong>22 Oct 2026</strong> · The National Archives acknowledges FOI request CAS-361652-D3X8X9 (corporate records, received 16 Oct). Reply due 13 Nov 2026. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0515</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a163b9bb8538edf\">email</a></li><li><strong>22 Oct 2026</strong> · Glamorgan Archives (ref 2026/4461) answers the preservation notice: its holdings are designated for permanent preservation and will not be destroyed; it holds no planning files; Planning Committee papers DCVG/C/4/36/76-77 and DCVG/C/4/36/94 are held. Four follow-up questions sent the same evening. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0516</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a1645f237df4972\">email</a></li><li><strong>22 Oct 2026</strong> · Follow-ups sent: clarification to Amgueddfa Cymru (FOI 2026-024/032/036); internal review asked of the Vale of Glamorgan Council for case 00211463 (no response by 19 Oct); reply to the Council's scrutiny officer; chaser to the RCT coroner's service (two points open since 26 Aug); reconsideration under EIR reg 11 asked of Historic England (26/04323). · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a164d701e8cac8f\">email</a></li><li><strong>22 Oct 2026</strong> · FOI request to The National Archives for the location of closed or Discovery records on Great House Farm (OS Glamorgan XLVII.6, Valuation Office field books IR 58). The receiving mail server rejected it; not delivered. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0517</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a164d6eee708c9a\">email</a></li><li><strong>22 Oct 2026</strong> · Section 50 complaint to the Information Commissioner's Office about the Ministry of Justice / HMCTS handling of request 260813002 (1988–1989 court records). ICO case reference IC-586450-N8N0. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0518</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a164d73591d629f\">email</a></li><li><strong>23 Oct 2026</strong> · BP replies to the 16 Oct preservation notice: it knows of no outstanding or live cause of action, refers to the 1987 Court of Appeal decision, does not confirm a preservation hold, and invites the interest, legal basis and relief sought to be set out. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0308</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a16814eff6e8660\">email</a></li><li><strong>23 Oct 2026</strong> · Cardiff Central Library replies on Bute X.6(12): the item is still held; staff found no information about the property in it, and no matches in the manuscript index; a scan only through Glamorgan Archives at a cost; detailed research only for a charge; an in-person visit offered. Two Bute catalogues attached. Fee asked; noted. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0341</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a16876a2f78ac5e\">email</a></li><li><strong>23 Oct 2026</strong> · The National Archives: internal review CAS-356384-B2F5L9, due 23 Oct, is still ongoing; decision expected by 20 Nov 2026. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0445</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a16882d4f515f19\">email</a></li><li><strong>23 Oct 2026</strong> · HM Land Registry logs the 20 Oct request as EIR F261029 and FOI F261030. Statutory deadline 17 Nov 2026. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0519</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a168c69031bff64\">email</a></li><li><strong>23 Oct 2026</strong> · Audit Wales acknowledges the information request as IR1038. <span class=\"ev-ref\">EV-0302</span> · <a href=\"https://email.bucklerfamily.estate/reference/1a168f453b3abea1\">email</a></li></ul></details></section><section class=\"research-addendum\" id=\"research-added-2026-10-22\"><h2>Added on research: 22 October 2026</h2><ul><li><strong>22 Oct 2026</strong> · Llandough Community Council meeting (remote only), Item 10: a request to pass the family’s contact details to people who remember the village between the 1950s and the 1990s, and to consider an interpretation board or plaque near the green for the 1,026 burials beneath Church View Close. Agenda issued 13 Oct 2026; minutes not yet published. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0513-llandough-community-council-agenda-22-october-2026-item-10/\">EV-0513</a> · <a href=\"/project-management/llandough-community-council-22-october-2026/\">Item 10 page</a></li></ul></section>",
